Included portions
-----------------

The Zig port of the PS4 PKG and PFS readers derives from the shadPS4 Emulator Project's
file_format and crypto code, as redistributed in https://github.com/xXJSONDeruloXx/ps4-pkg-tools:

    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2024 shadPS4 Emulator Project
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

The ZArchive (.zar) writer, once it lands, will be a port of ZArchive by Exzap (MIT licensed):

    https://github.com/Exzap/ZArchive

Qt 6 is used under the GPLv3 option and is linked dynamically.

Vendored from kleinergoo7/pkg2zar commit 26abc7504b401e7aaff4caf222d0e85ce999ba4d; core only, built with Zig 0.16.0.

Local divergence: in Source.sceEntryData, NP entry decryption reads the full 16-byte-aligned
cipher block from the PKG (including its stored padding bytes) instead of zero-padding the
final block. Upstream zero-pads only the stored bytes, which yields a wrong final block: AES-CBC
diffusion mixes the padding into every decrypted byte of that block. The full-block read is
confirmed by the SHA-1 self-check embedded in npbind.dat (its last 20 bytes hash the first 512).
